  "configuration_id": "config_045",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is config_016: multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, ViT-L, avgpool, weighted fusion, with the best validation accuracy (0.542) at moderate cost (2.94 GPU hours). Transformer aggregation and concat fusion have underperformed in comparable settings, so the most promising remaining uncertainty is whether scgpt is the best RNA encoder when paired with the best image encoder, aggregation, and fusion. config_045 tests this directly by keeping ViT-L, avgpool, and weighted fusion while replacing scgpt with scvi_n200. It is expected to have comparable or slightly lower cost than config_016 because the ViT-L and aggregation pipeline likely dominate training time, making it an efficient exploitation step that can either improve the best accuracy or confirm scgpt as the preferred RNA encoder."
}

